{"text": "Category G is Autism Spectrum Disorder. The educational description is: A lifelong neurodevelopmental disability associated with differences in social communication and interaction, patterns of interests or behaviour, and sensory responsiveness. Presentation and support needs vary widely. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Sofia Martinez, who is in Grade 3 and uses she/her pronouns. Sofia is autistic and uses fluent speech, scripting, drawing, and a visual schedule. She meets grade-level academic standards but needs explicit support for flexibility, social communication, and sensory regulation. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Sofia, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Sofia’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-G-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.7, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "G", "start": 0.7125, "end": 1.125, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.1375, "end": 1.3625, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Autism", "start": 1.375, "end": 1.8875, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 20}, {"text": "Spectrum", "start": 1.9, "end": 2.4125, "start_char": 21, "end_char": 29}, {"text": "Disorder", "start": 2.425, "end": 3.0875, "start_char": 30, "end_char": 38}, {"text": "The", "start": 